<title>THAILAND: Thai central bank plans to issue more 1997 bonds.</title>
<headline>Thai central bank plans to issue more 1997 bonds.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank of Thailand governor Rerngchai Marakanond said on Tuesday the central bank plans to issue more bonds next year to absorb an expected increase in market liquidity.</p>
<p>The money supply is expected to be very high next year in anticipation of the establishment of an increasing number of pension funds from private and public agencies, he said.</p>
<p>&quot;The new pension funds from the private and public sectors will increase the money supply in the system. The BOT will issue bonds to absorb the expected surplus liquidity,&quot; he told reporters.</p>
<p>The governor did not elaborate on the planned bond issue.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
